the Chow [W5, W6, W7] requires having W5 or W7 in the hand, which is missing. Passing avoids invalid moves.\nReason: To form a valid Chow [W5, W6, W7], the player must have two of the three tiles. While holding W6 and W7, the absence of W5 makes this action invalid. Passing is the only logical choice.\nAnswer: Pass"}
